# Build context is the repo root (`docker buildx build ... -f
# server-go/Dockerfile .`), so this is the .dockerignore Docker reads.
# server-go/.dockerignore is NOT consulted for that build — it only
# applies if someone builds with server-go/ as the context.
#
# node_modules must be excluded or the release build breaks outright:
# the web-build stage runs `npm ci` and then `COPY web/ ./` on top of
# it. A local pnpm install makes web/node_modules/@base-ui/react a
# symlink, npm ci makes it a real directory, and BuildKit refuses the
# overlay with "cannot replace to directory ... with file". That made
# `make ship` fail on any machine that had run a local web build.
# Excluding it is also what the Dockerfile already assumes: it copies
# package.json + package-lock.json and installs deps itself.
**/node_modules

# Build outputs — regenerated inside the image, and .next in particular
# would clobber the cache mount the web-build stage relies on.
web/.next
web/out
dist
server-go/internal/web/dist

.git
.github
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Local-only files that must never reach a published image.
*.local.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
